<title>GERMANY: Veba denies interest in Bremer Vulkan.</title>
<headline>Veba denies interest in Bremer Vulkan.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German utility Veba AG on Wednesday denied newspaper reports that it was interested in buying parts of bankrupt shipyard group Bremer Vulkan Verbund AG.</p>
<p>&quot;The press reports in question lie clearly in the area of speculation,&quot; a Veba spokesman said.</p>
<p>German business daily Handelsblatt reported that Veba and steel group Thyssen AG were interested in taking over Bremer Vulkan to pick up loss carryovers worth between three and four billion marks and thus cut their own tax exposure.</p>
<p>Thyssen has also denied it wants to take over Vulkan.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
